{
 "version": 6,
 "about": [
  "Explicit map from QuantiSheet AI Takeoff result lines to the human takeoff groups (Group_ID) in the reviewer's Aiken_Human_vs_AI_Comparison.xlsx, sheet Mapping. Read by tools/aiken_eval.py; the scorer itself does no fuzzy matching.",
  "An AI line key is '<engine>:<name>' where engine is rooms, pipes, civil, devices, ducts, steel (counts EA, beam LF, weight LB), footings (CY) or schedules (schedule keys counted on the plans: 'schedules:P-1 WALL HUNG LAVATORY', 'schedules:Doors', 'schedules:Hardware set 1.0', 'schedules:Light C 2X4 TROFFER', 'schedules:Plant Ab ...'), finishes (per finish code from the rooms and the finish schedule: 'finishes:Floor EPX' SF, 'finishes:Base RB' LF, 'finishes:Ceiling ACT / GB' SF, 'finishes:Wall finish PT-1 / PT-2' SF) or walls (one floor plan per level: 'walls:Wall Type 2A' LF per wall type, 'walls:Exterior Walls' LF of the outer face loop, '... wall area' SF where a height is known) and name is the measurement group exactly as AI Takeoff names it, e.g. 'pipes:1/2\" CW' or 'civil:6\" PVC sanitary, depth unknown'.",
  "Rules are tried in order: every 'key' (exact) rule first, then every 'regex' rule (Python re.search, so anchor with ^ and $). The first rule that matches wins; one AI line maps to at most one group, a group may collect many lines (summed).",
  "'group' may also be 'R<row>' for one human row the reviewer left unmapped (e.g. R123); such a row then scores as its own group.",
  "Lines matched by 'info' are listed in ai_lines.csv but not counted as AI lines the human doesn't carry.",
  "'groups' holds per-group unit conversions: when the AI unit differs from the human unit, human qty x factor gives the human qty in that unit (the reviewer's conversions, 'compared on base QUANTITY pre-waste').",
  "Quantities only. No prices, no cost data.",
  "v4 (Oct 26): 0.13.8 roof, site, earthwork, flex duct and pipe-drop lines mapped. Roof area is compared on plan SF (the human standing-seam line matches plan area); fill maps to the human Fill row (R743).",
  "v4: wall assemblies (round 5) mapped where the human row is clearly the same wall type's material.",
  "v5: the workbook's Division 01 lines (general:..., 1 LS each) map to the human general rows R12-R18.",
  "v5: two-ceiling rooms split by the RCP grid map like their codes; the gypsum board ceiling SF joins the human all-ceilings group (it carries the GB ceiling rows)."
 ],
 "groups": {
  "H05-HSS4": {
   "alt": {
    "EA": 0.0079902
   },
   "note": "human LBS / (12.21 lb/ft x 10'-3\" column height) = column count"
